# === Local scratch (untracked, not part of the repo) ===
# Contents are scratch, with two exceptions that ARE part of the repo: the standalone
# service-label diagnostics and its runbook section. test/docker-win/Dockerfile does
# `COPY misc/`, so a fresh clone must contain at least the script or the image build fails.


misc/*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# test/ is IGNORE-BY-DEFAULT with a small allowlist.
#
# Most of what lives under test/docker-win/ must never be committed: multi-GB
# baked binaries (otelcol-contrib.exe, node.zip, otel-dotnet.zip), host-installed
# node_modules (npm-global/, otel-node/, nodeapp/node_modules/) and vendor
# installers. The telemetry-SHIPPING harnesses are also left out on purpose -
# they need those binaries plus live Coralogix keys, so committing them would put
# files in the repo that nobody can run from a clean clone.
#
# Allowlisted: the two SELF-CONTAINED ASSERTING harnesses. They have expected
# results, exit non-zero on failure, and are what CI or a reviewer would actually
# run. Everything they need is either in the repo already (deploy/) or built by
# the Dockerfile.
#
# Re-including inside an ignored tree has to be done level by level - git will not
# descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so negating a file inside one has no effect.
test/*
# Fixture-only unit suites: no baked binaries, no keys, run from a clean clone.
!test/Test-SupervisorConfigWriter.ps1
!test/Test-ServiceInstrumenters.ps1
!test/docker-win
test/docker-win/*

# Runtime-classification unit tests. Fixture-only: no Docker, no IIS, no elevation, no keys,
# about a second to run - the fastest gate on the detection rules, and the only thing that
# catches misc/Test-CxInstrumentation.ps1's inlined copy drifting from deploy/Resolve-IISAppRuntime.ps1.
!test/Test-ResolveIISAppRuntime.ps1

# PM2 topology / service-hosted-daemon unit tests. Same deal - fixture-only, stubs the machine
# probes and Task Scheduler, runs unelevated in about a second. This is the only gate on the rules
# that decide whether a service-hosted PM2 is found at all, which a Windows container cannot
# easily reproduce (it would need a LOCAL SERVICE-owned node-windows daemon).
!test/Test-Pm2Topology.ps1

# Offline diagnostics matrix - no keys, no network (Run-DoctorTest.ps1).
!test/docker-win/Run-DoctorTest.ps1
!test/docker-win/Dockerfile.doctor
!test/docker-win/entrypoint.doctor.ps1
!test/docker-win/break-state.ps1

# Full deploy loop over the IIS shape matrix (Run-E2ELoop.ps1). Its Coralogix
# phase needs keys, but every other phase runs offline.
!test/docker-win/Run-E2ELoop.ps1
!test/docker-win/Dockerfile.e2e
!test/docker-win/entrypoint.e2e.ps1

!test/docker-win/README.md

# Artifacts the deploy scripts PRODUCE on the host they run on. The package is an
# allowlist (Build-DeploymentPackage.ps1 $required), so these are never shipped -
# they just appear next to the scripts after a run.
deploy/config.recommended.yaml
deploy/agent-doctor.*
deploy/*.jsonl
deploy/install-agent*.log
deploy/uninstall-agent*.log
deploy/install-agent-status.json
deploy/detect-workloads.json

# Artifacts collected FROM a host and pulled back here for analysis (doctor.json,
# cx-inst.json, detect output) plus any report written about them. Host-specific and
# often carrying real site/app names - never committed. Both spellings, so a rename
# of the misspelled folder stays ignored.
artifacs/
artifacts/
